//@version=6
indicator("UDB-ORB TSLA v3.9.8 - A1/B1/C1/C2/D1 Profiles", shorttitle="UDB-ORB v3.9.8", overlay=true, max_labels_count=500, max_lines_count=500)

// v3.9.8 2026-08-11 — PD-LEVEL EXIT NOW WATCHES BOTH SIDES. New input "Levels AHEAD of entry only",
//     DEFAULT UNTICKED, which drops the guard that a level must lie ahead of the entry. A level the
//     trade already broke now triggers too, so closing back through it is an exit ("you lost the
//     level"). Nothing else in the rule changed — small body, reject candle, ranking below stop /
//     target / partial / runner, and it still does not arm the reversal.
//     WHY: on 2026-08-04 and 2026-08-11 the short triggered ~$0.33 below PDC and was immediately
//     reclaimed; ahead-only is structurally blind to that. Of the four legs across the three days
//     the user flagged (08-04, 08-05, 08-11), three had no level ahead within reach at all and the
//     08-11 reversal was above ALL FOUR levels, so no ahead-only buffer of any size could act.
//     ADOPTED BY USER CALL AGAINST THE MEASUREMENT — the honest numbers, 2022-01-03..2026-08-10
//     per unit, unticked vs ticked: A1 485.6/502.0, B1 558.3/575.9, C1 556.4/573.2, D1 480.3/483.5.
//     B1 by year: 2022 -21.2 / 2023 -5.1 / 2024 -4.8 / 2025 -3.4 / 2026 +17.0. Win rate 46.2->44.2%.
//     Four of five years are worse and 2026 — the only year that gains — is also the only year the
//     motivating days came from, which is the known regime-trap signature. Tick the box to revert.
//     The tag zone stays 0.05: widening it changes NOTHING on those three days (identical at 0.05,
//     0.10 and 0.20) while costing a further ~$41/unit.
//
// v3.9.7 2026-08-11 — HALF-DAY SESSIONS NOW FLATTEN ON THEIR OWN LAST BAR. One line of session logic;
//     no profile, entry, exit or PD-level behaviour touched. `session.islastbar_regular` was meant to
//     cover the early close and simply does not fire on TSLA's 12:55 final bar, so the day-after-
//     Thanksgiving sessions emitted no EOD exit at all. In the v3.9.6 STRATEGY exports that left the
//     position orphaned into the NEXT session, closed a full day late by the "EOD flat" safety net:
//     2012-11-23, 2018-11-23 (all four profiles) and 2017-11-24 (C1) — the 2018 one a -$121.20 short
//     carried through a three-day weekend on a chart that is supposed to be flat every night.
//     The session's real end is now read from the daily bar (`time_close("D")` = 13:00 on an early
//     close, 16:00 otherwise), which matches orb_engine.py's `last_ts_by_date`. FULL SESSIONS ARE
//     TRADE-FOR-TRADE UNCHANGED: on a normal day the new condition lands on the 15:55 bar, which the
//     15:50 EOD rule had already claimed. Only ~3 sessions in 14 years differ.
//
// v3.9.6 2026-08-10 — THE PD-LEVEL TAG-AND-REJECT EXIT IS NOW ON BY DEFAULT (`pdxOn` false -> true).
//     ONE INPUT DEFAULT CHANGED, no logic edited. The rule itself, its ranking below the stop / target /
//     partial / runner, and its refusal to arm the reversal are all exactly as shipped in v3.9.4.
//     WHY: measured TV-natively on C1 over 2025-08-11..2026-08-10 by exporting the SAME script twice,
//     once with the box ticked and once without (the two exports are otherwise trade-for-trade identical,
//     260 of 260 entries matching to the cent, so the delta is the rule and nothing else):
//         ON  $17,554   PF 1.76   win rate 55.2%
//         OFF $13,623   PF 1.52   win rate 50.4%
//     = +$3,932 (+29%), worst single trade unchanged, positive in both year-cells (2025 +$1,786 /
//     2026 +$2,145). The 54 fires are right 38 times (70%): they save $6,195 and give up $2,530, and one
//     of them pays twice — 2025-09-10 cut a primary at -$18 instead of a -$154 BE Stop, and because a
//     PD-Level exit does NOT arm the reversal it also skipped the -$266 reversal that followed.
//     CAVEAT, unchanged: the 0.25 body threshold was fitted in-sample on this same span with NO holdout,
//     the plateau is flat rather than peaked (see the knob's tooltip — the old note that D1 preferred 0.15
//     did not survive a full sweep), and TV charges zero commission and zero
//     slippage. Set "Enable PD-level tag-and-reject exit" OFF to get the v3.9.3 baseline back.
//
// v3.9.5 2026-08-10 — THE OR / TRIGGER LINES NOW BEHAVE LIKE THE PD LINES. Cosmetic only: no entry, exit,
//     stop, target, reversal, day-skip or alert rule changed, so this version is trade-for-trade IDENTICAL
//     to v3.9.4 (which is itself identical to v3.9.3 with the experimental exit left OFF).
//     OR High / OR Low / Long Trigger / Short Trigger were plot(style_linebr) — one continuous series that
//     TradingView joins from the last bar of one session to the first bar of the next, so on a multi-day
//     chart yesterday's aqua/lime/red levels ran on into today. They are now four LINE OBJECTS per session:
//     opened on that day's OR bar, extended only to that day's own bars, then never touched again. Each
//     carries a small right-end tag ("OR H 331.20", "OR L 328.40", "LONG > 331.55", "SHORT < 328.05") so
//     no legend is needed. Triggers are DASHED to separate them from the solid OR boundaries at a glance.
//     History is bounded by "Days of OR / trigger segments to keep" (default 10), the same guard the PD
//     segments use, so the 500-line / 500-label caps stay safe. Skipped days (vol / wide-OR) draw nothing,
//     exactly as before. Two new Display inputs: "Tag the OR / trigger lines" and the days-to-keep count.
//
//     ALSO IN v3.9.5 — THE CHART STATUS LINE IS NOW READABLE. TradingView echoes every input value after
//     the script name, which on this script was a ~40-number wall ("... 15 50 09:30 12 0 8 20 4.92 10 1 60
//     0 1 2.14 0.25 1 14 2 0.55 ..." running off the right edge). Every input now carries
//     `display=display.none` EXCEPT `profile`, so the status line reads just
//         UDB-ORB v3.9.7   A1 - Adaptive + Peak-Trail
//     The inputs themselves are UNCHANGED — same names, defaults, groups and tooltips in the settings
//     dialog; only their on-chart echo is suppressed, and nothing about the logic can move. The stats table
//     stays the place to read live values. Zero-code equivalent if you ever want them back on one chart:
//     Chart settings -> Status line -> "Indicator arguments". The Pine flag is better for a chart you look
//     at every day; the checkbox is per-chart and easy to lose.
//
// v3.9.4 2026-08-10 — TWO CHANGES, both to the prior-day-level feature added in v3.9.3.
//
// (1) THE LINES ARE NOW ONE SEGMENT PER DAY. v3.9.3 drew them with plot(style_stepline), which runs
//     continuously across the whole chart and puts a vertical riser at every session boundary — so
//     yesterday's level visually bled into today and the risers looked like levels of their own. Each
//     session now gets its own four line objects, opened on the first RTH bar and extended only to that
//     session's last bar. Nothing carries into the next day. A small tag ("PDH 331.20") now rides the
//     RIGHT END of each segment, sitting just ABOVE the line, so every line is self-identifying without
//     the legend. History is bounded by "Days of prior-day segments to keep" (default 10) — older days'
//     objects are deleted, so this cannot starve the trade labels of TradingView's 500-object caps.
//
// (2) NEW OPTIONAL EXIT: "PD-level tag-and-reject" — DEFAULT OFF, so this version is trade-for-trade
//     IDENTICAL to v3.9.3 out of the box. When enabled, an open position is flattened at the close of a
//     bar that (a) tags a prior-day level lying AHEAD of the trade, (b) closes rejected back off it, and
//     (c) has a SMALL BODY (|close-open| / (high-low) < the threshold). The body filter is the whole
//     result: the unfiltered rule is one of the worst things ever tested on this system (-$3,800..-$5,500
//     over 5 years, every profile), while the same rule restricted to small-bodied bars is +$1,248 (A1),
//     +$2,983 (B1, 5/5 years), +$3,487 (C1, 5/5 years), +$755 (D1). A doji or pin that runs into the
//     level and cannot close through it is the signal; a big decisive candle at the level is just a trend
//     bar and price continues. Mirrors the Python enhancement `pd_level_exit` + `max_body_frac`.
//     NOT ADOPTED: the 0.25 threshold was chosen in-sample over all five years with no holdout, the
//     plateau is flat, not peaked, and the effect is dead by 0.35. Forward-validate
//     before turning it on with money. See docs/BE_STOP_ANALYSIS.md S32c.
//
// v3.9.3 2026-08-09 — PRIOR-DAY LEVELS (PDH / PDL / PDC / PDO) ADDED, DIAGNOSTIC ONLY.
// Four new plots + an input group "Prior-Day Levels". NOTHING in the trading logic reads them:
// no entry, exit, stop, target, reversal or day-skip condition changed, no alert text changed,
// so this version is trade-for-trade IDENTICAL to v3.9.2. Purpose: eyeball on the chart whether
// ORB failures (BE stops in particular — 87% of losses) cluster at a prior-day level.
// LEGEND — deliberately four different colours AND four different line patterns so each one is
// identifiable in a screenshot:
//     PDH = MAGENTA / fuchsia, thick SOLID step line     (prior day HIGH)
//     PDL = BLUE  #2962FF,     thick SOLID step line     (prior day LOW)
//     PDC = WHITE,             thin DOTTED (circles)     (prior day CLOSE)
//     PDO = ORANGE,            thin CROSS / x marks      (prior day OPEN)
// Right-edge labels ("PDH 331.20" ...) are on by default and re-use 4 label objects (moved, never
// re-created), so they cost nothing against TradingView's 500-label cap.
// PRIOR ART: the Python enhancement `pdh_pdl_filter` (require the break close to be beyond PDH/PDL
// when the level sits near the trigger) is BUILT and default OFF — it barely triggers on TSLA
// (docs/BE_STOP_ANALYSIS.md sect.6). PDC and PDO have never been tested in any form.
//
// v3.9.2 2026-08-09 — DEFAULT PROFILE C1 -> A1 (input default only; no logic/alert/plot change).
// Bumped in lockstep with the STRATEGY v3.9.2, which also switches its "Option expiration" default
// from '+0 days' to 'Friday (weekly)'. THIS INDICATOR HAS NO OPTIONS INPUTS — its alerts are plain
// text, the options webhook JSON lives only in the strategy — so the expiry change does not apply
// here; only the profile default moved, so chart and strategy agree on A1 out of the box.
// WHY A1: the 2026-08-09 options expiry audit (see the strategy header for the full note) found
// TSLA listed FRIDAY-ONLY expiries until 2026-02-02, so the published "0DTE" options figures were
// really weekly; re-priced properly, A1 leads on options in both measured windows and is the only
// profile positive in the flat Jan-May 2026 stretch. B1 is the WORST on options despite being a
// traded shares profile — the shares ranking and the options ranking are NOT the same.
//
// v3.9.1 2026-07-28 — DOCUMENTATION ONLY (no logic, no input, no alert, no plot change). Records a
//   concept tested and REJECTED 2026-07-28, so it is not re-proposed from the chart:
//   IMMEDIATE REVERSAL ON THE BE-STOP BAR — flip at the same 5m close the BE stop fills at,
//   instead of waiting for a close back through the raw opposite OR boundary (the current rule).
//   Asked from a live chart where the flip would have worked; built as the Python enhancement
//   reversal_capture.immediate_on_be_stop (default OFF) and swept on ALL FIVE profiles.
//   It roughly DOUBLES the reversal count (198 -> 374 over 5yr) while total reversal P&L FALLS
//   (+145.6 -> +79.8/unit) — the ~176 extra flips are collectively net-negative. The best variant
//   beat baseline on 2024-2026 WINDOW TOTALS in every profile (A1 +17.6, B1 +17.6, C1 +5.7,
//   C2 +28.0, D1 +23.4) — but per YEAR it loses 2022, 2023 AND 2024 in every profile:
//     delta/unit vs base, sum of A1+B1+C1+C2+D1:
//     2022 -78.8 | 2023 -151.7 | 2024 -56.0 | 2025 +109.5 | 2026YTD +38.9   (2022-23 = true OOS)
//   The whole "edge" is 2025. Trailing 2 months negative in all five (A1/B1/D1 -2.8, C1 -3.5,
//   C2 -0.2); D1's 5yr maxDD degrades -56.1 -> -66.6. Same 2025-only regime signature that killed
//   the midline-trigger reversal (v-note below / config.yaml). Profile choice cannot rescue it:
//   all five share ONE entry engine and differ only in the runner exit, so the flip lands on the
//   identical set of BE-stop bars (hence near-identical deltas on A1/B1/D1).
//   DO NOT RE-ADD. The OR-break wait is a FILTER, not latency — crossing the whole range is what
//   distinguishes a genuine failed breakout from chop INSIDE the range, and the reversal's own
//   stop is only meaningful once price has crossed it. (Structural note: a BE-stop fill often
//   lands inside/below the OR, which would put the normal reversal stop on the WRONG side of
//   entry and let the risk-parity cap inflate size absurdly.)
//   Reproduce: python scripts/immediate_reversal_test.py --profiles all --years [--windows|--detail]
//   Full analysis: docs/BE_STOP_ANALYSIS.md §31.
// v3.9 2026-07-26 — ENTRY CUTOFF ADOPTED (default ON, 12:00): loss-anatomy on 5 years of trades
//   showed post-noon entries are a net-NEGATIVE cohort (the 12:00-13:00 lunch hour is the toxic
//   pocket; losing stops die in ~30min while winners run for hours). No NEW entries — primary or
//   reversal — after 12:00; open positions still manage to their normal exits. Verified on
//   A1/B1/C1/D1 incl 2022-23 OOS: WR up in every tested year-cell, net +3-4% (B1 5yr +463.4 vs
//   +450.7/unit), worst day never worse (2025's improves −10.9 vs −12.0). Python twin:
//   enhancements.time_window {start 09:35, end 12:00} enabled in the A1/B1/C1/D1 + default yamls.
//   Knob re-sweep same day: stop cap $5, BE trigger 0.55, BE trail $0.25 all confirmed optimal
//   (BE 0.85 buys ~+4pt WR but costs $65/3yr and deeper tails — not taken).
// v3.8 2026-07-25 — version bump in lockstep with the STRATEGY's "Option quantity mode" input
//   (options webhook can omit quantity so TradersPost's dollar-based position sizing decides the
//   contract count — the +49-63% fixed-$ sizing finding). THIS INDICATOR NEEDED NO CHANGE (its
//   alerts are plain text, no webhook JSON). Bumped only so chart + alerts show matching names.
// v3.7 2026-07-24 — CONFIGURABLE SHARE QUANTITY (user request, mirrors the Option-contracts input):
//   new "Share quantity (shares per 1.0 unit)" input (default 25 = the old hardcoded scale).
//   INDICATOR: entry / reversal / partial alerts now state the exact share count to place
//   (reversal = risk-parity scaled, partial = partialPct of the position); summary table adds a
//   "Net @ N sh" dollar row. STRATEGY: the old "Shares per 'unit'" input is RENAMED "Share quantity"
//   — order qty and webhook JSON quantity = Units Per Trade x this (reversal: risk-parity x this).
//   Keep the indicator and strategy inputs EQUAL. No trade-logic change anywhere.
// v3.6 2026-07-23 — D1 EXIT MODE OPTION (user request, like the C2 formula input): new "D1 Exit
//   mode" input — "Partial TP + ATR Trail" (default, the original D1) vs "FULL EXIT AT ATR TRAIL":
//   nothing is taken at the adaptive TP (its touch only ARMS the trail), 100% exits on the TRADE
//   TASTIC flip — one alert / one order, so it also suits platforms that cannot split exits.
//   Tested (per unit, fixed trail, close-stop) full-trail vs partial: 2024 +39.7 vs +38.4 |
//   2025 +85.2 vs +72.2 | 2026YTD +179.0 vs +162.3 -> full-trail wins ALL THREE (3yr +304 vs +273;
//   B1 ref +268) at a slightly deeper 2025 worst day (-13.6 vs -12.0) and ~1pt lower WR.
//   Python twin: tsla_config_D1.yaml with partial_qty_pct: 0.0.
// v3.5 2026-07-23 — C2 TAKE-PROFIT FORMULA CHANGED (user request): C2's target is now the OPEN
//   BAR's High - Low (= OR width, no floor/scale) instead of the fixed $2. Per unit, close-stop,
//   OR-width vs fixed-$2: 2022 +29.7 vs +42.9 | 2023 +82.3 vs +88.8 | 2024 +36.6 vs -23.1 |
//   2025 +38.3 vs -0.3 | 2026YTD +111.7 vs +49.0  => 5yr +298.6 vs +157.3 (~2x), POSITIVE EVERY
//   YEAR (the fixed $2 was net-NEGATIVE 2024 and flat 2025 under the close stop). WR drops
//   (46-50% vs 50-63%): fewer tiny banked wins, bigger targets on wide-OR days. TP floors $1/$2
//   tested: no effect. The old behavior stays selectable: "C2 Take-Profit formula" = Fixed $.
// v3.4 2026-07-23 — D1 SHORT-SIDE FIX (user-caught same day on the live chart): the original
//   TRADE TASTIC script has ONE line — a SHORT must exit on the red->green flip of the SAME
//   HHV(high - mult*ATR) line, not on an invented mirrored LLV(low + mult*ATR) line. On 2026-07-23's
//   short the true flip was 10:35 (close 324.30 > TS 319.48); the mirror exited 11:55. Fixed in this
//   indicator, the v3.4 STRATEGY, and the Python engine (all now single-line, longs unchanged).
//   CORRECTED numbers, per unit, D1 vs B1: 2024 +38.4 vs +20.2 | 2025 +72.2 vs +102.8 |
//   2026YTD +153.9 vs +138.0 -> 3yr ~tie (+264 vs +261). D1 wins 2024+2026, loses 2025;
//   still experimental / NOT adopted — VWAP (B1/C1) stays the traded runner exit.
// v3.3 2026-07-23 — NEW PROFILE D1 (experimental, for side-by-side comparison — NOT adopted):
//   D1 = Adaptive TP + 25% partial + "TRADE TASTIC" ATR TRAIL runner (B1's engine, the
//   runner exits on the TRADE TASTIC color flip instead of the VWAP cross). Python twin:
//   config/tsla_config_D1.yaml (enhancement atr_trail_exit). (v3.3's short side + numbers were
//   the buggy mirror — superseded by the v3.4 fix above.)

// v3.2 2026-07-23 — version bump in lockstep with the STRATEGY's partial-as-order option (Shares mode:
// the 25% partial can fire as an opposite-side order JSON — long -> action=Sell qty N, short -> Buy — for
// execution platforms whose action=exit ALWAYS flattens the whole position and ignores quantity; the
// platform must NET, not reverse). THIS INDICATOR NEEDED NO LOGIC CHANGE: its alerts are plain text.
// PARTIAL VALUE (tested 2026-07-23, per unit): forced one-time exit AT the TP costs most of the edge
// (B1 2025 +38.9 vs +102.8 w/ partial; C1 2025 +9.0 vs +77.4) — the money is the 75% runner, not the WR.
// Partial % = 0 (nothing off, 100% rides the runner) beat the 25% partial in 2025 AND 2026 on all profiles
// (A1 2026 +188.4 vs +167.8) at ~2-4pt lower WR; ~equal 2024 A1/C1, worse B1 2024 (+14.5 vs +20.2). It is
// the best SINGLE-EXIT fallback when a partial order can't work; 25% partial stays the adopted default.

// v3.1 2026-07-21 — version bump in lockstep with the STRATEGY's Options-alert fix (the strategy's
// Options-mode 25% partial sent alert_message=na -> TV emitted the literal "{{strategy.order.alert_message}}"
// placeholder). THIS INDICATOR NEEDED NO LOGIC CHANGE: its alerts are plain-text alert()/alertcondition()
// messages (no webhook placeholder). Bumped only so chart + alerts show matching v3.1 names.

// STATUS 2026-07-19 (validation update) — CORRECTED 2026-07-24: the rival "3-bot" concept (15m-OR long
// ATM ±50% + 30-min time stop, from the SPX system) originally showed +$45,916 @1ct on TSLA — that was
// ENTIRELY the bar-START pricing lookahead. Barclose-corrected on the same OPRA quotes: TSLA 3-bot is
// NEGATIVE (BOT1 -$2,295 @1ct 2022-26, WR 44%; spread bots all negative too) — UDB stays the TSLA
// system, now unambiguously. Credit spreads DON'T work on TSLA (thin credits, $2.50 strikes, weekly
// expiry) — don't sell them here. (The old day-of-week claims here predate the barclose correction —
// see the corrected UDB options stats in docs/TRADERSPOST_OPTIONS.md before using them.)
// The SPX system lives in SEPARATE files: SPX_ORB_3BOT_v1(.pine/_strategy.pine).
// STATUS 2026-07-13: ONE indicator, FOUR selectable profiles (fires ALERTS; identical logic to the v3
// STRATEGY). TSLA 5-minute, RTH, OR start 09:30 (selectable). Fires ALERTS + a PER-UNIT summary table;
// the STRATEGY carries the sizing ($10,000 account / 25 shares default). Same entry engine, ADOPTED
// close-triggered stops (exitOnClose ON), vol/OR gates, risk-parity reversal for all. Differ ONLY in exit:
//   A1 = Adaptive TP + 25% partial + PEAK-TRAIL runner   (Max Stop $5)
//   B1 = Adaptive TP + 25% partial + VWAP-CROSS runner   (Max Stop $5)
//   C1 = ATR-target (0.25x14d ATR) + 25% partial + VWAP  (Max Stop $6)   <- best PF
//   C2 = OR-WIDTH target (open bar H-L), FULL exit (no partial/runner) (Max Stop $5)  [was fixed $2 pre-v3.5]
//  ADOPTED RESULTS (close-triggered stop = exitOnClose ON; net per 1 UNIT; x25 = strategy on $10k, x100 = @100sh):
//  FULL 2022-2026 -> A1 +432.7/u (+108% on $10k), B1 +450.3/u (+113%), C1 +414.8/u (+104%), C2 +175.3/u (+44%).
//  PF: A1 1.22 / B1 1.23 / C1 1.22 / C2 1.12.   MaxDD on $10k: A1 -16% / B1 -19% / C1 -19% / C2 -17%.
//  USER TRADES B1 (max net) + C1 (best PF/DD balance). CLOSE-triggered stop = +42-46% net vs the old wick
//  stop, DD -40%, and 2024 FLIPS to a profit (OOS-confirmed on 2022-23). Set exitOnClose OFF for the old wick.
//  5m OR is CONFIRMED optimal (15m OR tested 2026-07-16 = worse in every profile/period: enters after the thrust).
//  OPTIONS (TradersPost 0DTE) live in the v3 STRATEGY, not here (this indicator has no orders/positions):
//    set Order asset=Options there. Works on ALL profiles (the 25% partial's webhook is auto-suppressed so
//    1 contract rides to the runner exit); default 2 contracts. Backtest @1ct, barclose
//    fills, 2025-01..2026-07-17 (UPDATED 2026-07-25 — now includes D1 and the OR-width C2):
//    A1 +$12,895 / D1 +$11,284 / B1 +$11,241 / C1 +$10,059 / C2 +$4,246. 2026 YTD ranking:
//    A1 +$8,971 > D1 +$7,499 > B1 +$5,840 > C1 +$4,628 > C2 +$2,417 — matches the shares ranking.
//    ^ THOSE ARE **WEEKLY** NUMBERS, NOT 0DTE (corrected 2026-08-09): TSLA listed FRIDAY-ONLY expiries
//    until 2026-02-02, so ~85% of that window could only ever have been priced on Friday contracts.
//    NOTE: the v3.5 OR-width TP flipped C2's options POSITIVE (old fixed-$2 C2 was -$967, "dead").
//    Expiry (strategy input): DEFAULT IS NOW 'Friday (weekly)' (strategy v3.9.2). On 2026 data, where
//    real 0DTE contracts finally exist, WEEKLY beats true-0DTE on 5 of 5 profiles across 3 independent
//    windows, at ~22% more premium; it also always resolves to a listed contract, whereas '+0 days'
//    silently rolls to 1DTE on Tue/Thu since TSLA has no dailies (unlike SPX).
//    CONCENTRATION WARNING: 91% of 2026's options P&L came from Jun-mid-Jul (34 of 143 trades).
//    Jan-May 2026 weekly @1ct: A1 +$785 ONLY, D1 +$462, C1 -$316, C2 -$387, B1 -$1,116 — i.e. five
//    months at ~$7/trade on ~$656 premium for the best profile. Size for a flat stretch, not for June.
//    This indicator's alerts stay human-readable text + per-profile alertcondition()s (no webhook JSON).
//=============================================================================================

// ==================== PROFILE ====================
profile = input.string("A1 · Adaptive + Peak-Trail", "Profile",
     options=["A1 · Adaptive + Peak-Trail", "B1 · Adaptive + VWAP", "C1 · ATR 0.25 + 25% Partial + VWAP", "C2 · OR-Width Full-Exit", "D1 · Adaptive + ATR-Trail (exp)"], group="Profile")
c2TPFormula = input.string("OR width (open bar High-Low)", "C2 Take-Profit formula", options=["OR width (open bar High-Low)", "Fixed $"], group="Profile", tooltip="ADOPTED v3.5 (default): C2's target = the OPEN BAR's High - Low (= OR width, no floor). vs the old fixed $2 (per unit, close-stop): 2024 +36.6 vs -23.1, 2025 +38.3 vs -0.3, 2026YTD +111.7 vs +49.0; 2022/23 slightly behind; 5yr ~2x and positive every year. 'Fixed $' = the pre-v3.5 C2 (uses the Fixed TP $ input).", display=display.none)
d1ExitMode = input.string("Full exit at ATR Trail", "D1 Exit mode", options=["Full exit at ATR Trail", "Partial TP + ATR Trail"], group="Profile", tooltip="D1 only. 'Full exit at ATR Trail' (DEFAULT since 2026-07-23; the Python forward test tracks it) = NOTHING is taken at the TP — its touch only ARMS the trail; 100% exits on the flip (one alert, one order; suits platforms that cannot split exits). 'Partial TP + ATR Trail' = the original D1: 25% off at the adaptive TP, 75% rides the flip. v3.6 test (per unit, fixed trail): full-trail beats the partial in all of 2024/25/26 (+39.7/+85.2/+179.0 vs +38.4/+72.2/+162.3) at a slightly deeper 2025 worst day (-13.6 vs -12.0).", display=display.none)
isA1 = str.startswith(profile, "A1")
isB1 = str.startswith(profile, "B1")
isC1 = str.startswith(profile, "C1")
isC2 = str.startswith(profile, "C2")
isD1 = str.startswith(profile, "D1")
tpModeSel  = isC2 ? (str.startswith(c2TPFormula, "Fixed") ? "Fixed" : "ORw") : isC1 ? "ATR" : "Adaptive"
d1FullTrail = isD1 and str.startswith(d1ExitMode, "Full")   // D1 full-trail: TP touch only arms; 100% exits on the flip
usePartial = not isC2
runnerVWAP = isB1 or isC1              // D1 = ATR chandelier trail runner (neither VWAP nor peak-trail)

// ==================== INPUTS ====================
grpS = "Session"
eodHour = input.int(15, "EOD Exit Hour", minval=0, maxval=23, group=grpS, display=display.none)
eodMin  = input.int(50, "EOD Exit Minute", minval=0, maxval=59, group=grpS, display=display.none)
orStart = input.string("09:30", "Opening Range start bar", options=["09:30", "09:45"], group=grpS, display=display.none)
entryCutOn = input.bool(true, "Entry cutoff — no NEW entries after the time below", group=grpS, tooltip="ADOPTED 2026-07-26 (default ON, 12:00): entries after noon were a net-NEGATIVE cohort in 5 years of trade data — the damage concentrates in the 12:00-13:00 lunch hour. Blocking NEW entries (primary AND reversal; open positions still manage to their normal exits) after 12:00: WR up in all 7 tested year-cells on B1/D1 (+A1/C1 confirmed), net +3-4% (B1 5yr +463 vs +451/unit), worst day never worse, 2025's improves. OFF = trade all day (pre-cutoff behavior).", display=display.none)
entryCutH  = input.int(12, "Entry Cutoff Hour", minval=9, maxval=15, group=grpS, display=display.none)
entryCutM  = input.int(0,  "Entry Cutoff Minute", minval=0, maxval=59, group=grpS, display=display.none)

grpR = "Risk / Regime Gates"
maxORWidth  = input.float(8.0,  "Max OR Width ($) — skip wider days", step=0.5, group=grpR, display=display.none)
volLookback = input.int(20,     "Volatility Lookback (days)", minval=2, group=grpR, display=display.none)
maxRvolPct  = input.float(4.92, "Max Prior Realised Daily Vol (%)", step=0.01, group=grpR, display=display.none)

grpE = "Entry"
bufferPctOR = input.float(10.0, "Breakout Buffer (% of OR width)", step=0.5, group=grpE, display=display.none)
tradeQty    = input.float(1.0,  "Units Per Trade", minval=0.01, group=grpE, display=display.none)
shareQty    = input.int(25,     "Share quantity (shares per 1.0 unit)", minval=1, group=grpE, tooltip="v3.7: your FIXED share size, configured here like the strategy's Option-contracts input. Primary trade = Units Per Trade x this (default 1.0 x 25 = 25 sh); the risk-parity reversal scales off it. Entry/reversal/partial ALERTS now carry the exact share quantity to place, and the summary table adds a dollar P&L row at this size. Matches the STRATEGY's 'Share quantity' input — keep the two equal.", display=display.none)
slippage    = input.float(0.10, "Slippage Per Unit (charged on each exit)", step=0.01, group=grpE, display=display.none)

grpX = "Exit tuning (which apply depends on the Profile)"
maxCapOverride  = input.float(0.0,  "Max Stop override ($, 0 = use profile: C1=6 else 5)", step=0.5, group=grpX, display=display.none)
adaptiveTPScale = input.float(1.0,  "Adaptive TP — OR Width Multiplier (A1/B1)", step=0.05, group=grpX, display=display.none)
adaptiveTPMin   = input.float(2.14, "Adaptive TP — Minimum Floor $ (A1/B1)", step=0.01, group=grpX, display=display.none)
atrTPMult       = input.float(0.25, "ATR TP Multiplier x 14d ATR (C1)", step=0.01, group=grpX, display=display.none)
atrTPMin        = input.float(1.0,  "ATR TP Floor $ (C1)", step=0.25, group=grpX, display=display.none)
atrPeriod       = input.int(14,     "ATR Period (daily bars, C1)", minval=2, group=grpX, display=display.none)
fixedTP         = input.float(2.0,  "Fixed TP $ (C2)", step=0.25, group=grpX, display=display.none)
beTrigger       = input.float(0.55, "BE Retrace Trigger (% of OR width)", step=0.05, group=grpX, display=display.none)
beTrailAmt      = input.float(0.25, "BE Trail Amount ($)", step=0.01, group=grpX, display=display.none)
partialPct      = input.float(25.0, "Partial Exit Quantity % (A1/B1/C1)", step=1.0, group=grpX, display=display.none)
runnerMult      = input.float(0.75, "Runner Peak-Trail x OR width (A1)", step=0.05, group=grpX, display=display.none)
vwapArmProfit   = input.float(1.0,  "VWAP Cross — arm after profit $ (B1/C1)", step=0.25, group=grpX, display=display.none)
ttAtrPeriod     = input.int(5,      "ATR Trail — ATR Period (D1)", minval=1, group=grpX, display=display.none)
ttHhvPeriod     = input.int(10,     "ATR Trail — HHV/LLV Period (D1)", minval=1, group=grpX, display=display.none)
ttMult          = input.float(2.5,  "ATR Trail — ATR Multiplier (D1)", step=0.1, group=grpX, tooltip="D1 runner exit = the 'TRADE TASTIC' chandelier: line = HHV(high - mult*ATR(period), hhv) for longs (mirrored for shorts); the line moves only on a bar that CLOSES beyond it AND extends (close > prev close); the runner exits when a bar CLOSES across the line. Mult sweep 1.5-3.5 tested 2026-07-23: no setting wins 2024+2025+2026 together.", display=display.none)
exitOnClose     = input.bool(true,  "Close-triggered stop (stop fires only when the bar CLOSES beyond the level)", group=grpX, tooltip="ADOPTED 2026-07-14 (default ON): the stop fires only on a CLOSE beyond the level and fills at the close — skipping wick fakeouts. Walk-forward: +42-46% net and ~40% smaller drawdown vs the wick stop over 2022-2026 (flips 2024 positive). The TP still fills on a favorable wick. OFF = the old wick (any-touch) resting stop.", display=display.none)
beRealistic     = input.bool(true,  "Realistic resting stop: a BE-retrace can't protect its own firing bar", group=grpX, tooltip="ON (default) = matches a real broker + Python stop_fill_mode 'resting': moving the stop to break-even on the bar close only rests from the NEXT bar, so a bar that both fires the BE-retrace AND crashes to the base SL fills at the base SL. OFF = the old optimistic look-ahead (over-reports net ~40-45%).", display=display.none)

grpC = "Entry Confirmation"
confirmBreakout    = input.bool(false, "Require confirmation candle (2-candle break)", group=grpC, display=display.none)
requireTrendCandle = input.bool(true,  "Confirmation candle must be with-trend", group=grpC, display=display.none)

grpV = "Reversal"
revQtyMult = input.float(2.0, "Reversal Size Multiplier (before risk cap)", step=0.5, group=grpV, display=display.none)
revRiskCap = input.float(6.0, "Reversal Dollar-Risk Cap ($, 0=off)", step=0.5, group=grpV, display=display.none)

grpU = "Display"
showLabels = input.bool(true, "Show Entry/Exit Labels", group=grpU, display=display.none)
showLevels = input.bool(true, "Show OR / Trigger Levels", group=grpU, display=display.none)
showLvlLbl = input.bool(true, "Tag the OR / trigger lines", group=grpU, tooltip="v3.9.5: draws a small 'OR H 331.20' / 'LONG > 331.55' tag at the RIGHT END of each day's segment. The two OR tags sit INSIDE the opening range and the two trigger tags OUTSIDE it, so the ORH/long pair and the ORL/short pair never overlap even when the buffer is a few cents.", display=display.none)
orKeep     = input.int(10, "Days of OR / trigger segments to keep", minval=1, maxval=60, group=grpU, tooltip="v3.9.5: the OR High / OR Low / Long / Short levels are now drawn as one SEGMENT PER DAY instead of one continuous plot, so they stop at that session's last bar. Each session costs 4 line objects + 4 label objects; older sessions are DELETED once this many days are on screen. TradingView caps lines and labels at 500 each, and the prior-day segments plus the trade labels share the same budget.", display=display.none)
showTable  = input.bool(true, "Show Summary Table", group=grpU, display=display.none)

grpP = "Prior-Day Levels (PDH / PDL / PDC / PDO)"
showPD    = input.bool(true, "Show prior-day levels", group=grpP, tooltip="DIAGNOSTIC ONLY (v3.9.3): these four lines are DRAWN, never traded — no entry, exit, stop, target or day-skip rule reads them, so turning them on cannot change a single trade. They are yesterday's completed RTH daily bar (Open/High/Low/Close) held flat across today. LEGEND: PDH = MAGENTA thick solid, PDL = BLUE thick solid, PDC = WHITE dotted, PDO = ORANGE dashed.", display=display.none)
showPDLbl = input.bool(true, "Tag the end of each day's line", group=grpP, tooltip="v3.9.4: draws a small 'PDH 331.20' tag just ABOVE the RIGHT END of each day's segment, so every line identifies itself on the chart without the legend. 4 tags per session, bounded by the 'days to keep' setting below.", display=display.none)
pdKeep    = input.int(10, "Days of prior-day segments to keep", minval=1, maxval=60, group=grpP, tooltip="v3.9.4: the lines are now drawn as one SEGMENT PER DAY (they no longer run across the whole chart). Each session costs 4 line objects + 4 label objects; older sessions are DELETED once this many days are on screen. Keep it modest (10-20) — TradingView caps both lines and labels at 500 per script, and the trade labels compete for the same budget.", display=display.none)
showPDH   = input.bool(true, "PDH — prior day HIGH (magenta, solid)", group=grpP, display=display.none)
showPDL   = input.bool(true, "PDL — prior day LOW (blue, solid)", group=grpP, display=display.none)
showPDC   = input.bool(true, "PDC — prior day CLOSE (white, dotted)", group=grpP, display=display.none)
showPDO   = input.bool(true, "PDO — prior day OPEN (orange, dashed)", group=grpP, display=display.none)

// ---- PD-LEVEL TAG-AND-REJECT EXIT (v3.9.4) — EXPERIMENTAL, DEFAULT OFF ----
grpPX = "PD-Level Exit (tag-and-reject)"
pdxOn      = input.bool(true, "Enable PD-level tag-and-reject exit", group=grpPX, tooltip="DEFAULT ON since v3.9.6 (it was OFF in v3.9.4-v3.9.5). Measured on C1 over 2025-08-11..2026-08-10 by exporting this script twice, ticked and unticked: $17,554 vs $13,623 = +$3,932 (+29%), PF 1.76 vs 1.52, win rate 55.2% vs 50.4%, worst trade unchanged, positive in both year-cells. The 54 fires are right 70% of the time. CAVEAT: the body threshold below was fitted in-sample on that same span with no holdout. Turn this OFF to get the v3.9.3 baseline back. ON: an open position is flattened at the close of a bar that tags a prior-day level, closes rejected back off it, AND has a small body (see below). Which levels count is set by \"Levels AHEAD of entry only\" — since v3.9.8 that box is UNTICKED, so levels on both sides of the entry qualify. Ranks BELOW the stop, the target, the partial and the runner trail — those all keep precedence, so this only ever fires on a bar nothing else claimed. It does NOT arm the reversal (only Base SL / BE Stop / BE Trail do), matching orb_engine.py.", display=display.none)
pdxMaxBody = input.float(0.25, "Max rejection-candle body (|C-O| / (H-L))", minval=0.01, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=grpPX, tooltip="THE KNOB THAT MATTERS, and it runs OPPOSITE to intuition. A big decisive candle closing back off the level is worthless — it is a trend bar that happens to touch a line, and price continues. What predicts a real rejection is a SMALL body: a doji or pin that runs into the level and cannot close through it. 5-year deltas: no filter (1.0) = -$3,796 to -$5,466 on every profile; 0.25 = +$1,248 A1 / +$2,983 B1 / +$3,487 C1 / +$755 D1. The 0.10-0.25 band is a flat plateau; 0.35 is +$207 and 0.40-0.50 are negative. A full D1 sweep (2022-2026, per unit, baseline 450.5) put 0.25 at the TOP of that plateau — 0.10 +4.9% / 0.15 +7.2% / 0.20 +7.0% / 0.25 +7.8% / 0.30 +0.6% — so 0.25 is right for all four profiles and the earlier note that D1 preferred 0.15 is withdrawn. D1 is simply the weakest beneficiary (+7.8% vs C1 +25.0 / B1 +21.1 / A1 +10.6).", display=display.none)
pdxZone    = input.float(0.05, "Tag zone (x today's TP distance)", minval=0.0, maxval=0.50, step=0.01, group=grpPX, tooltip="How close the bar's extreme must come to the level to count as a tag, as a fraction of the adaptive TP distance shown in the stats table. 0.05 of a $3.74 TP distance = about 19 cents.", display=display.none)
pdxLevels  = input.string("All four (PDO/PDH/PDL/PDC)", "Which levels may trigger it", options=["All four (PDO/PDH/PDL/PDC)", "PDH + PDL only", "PDC only"], group=grpPX, tooltip="All four is the validated default. PDC-only and PDH/PDL-only were both swept WITHOUT the body filter and lost on every profile; they have not been re-swept with it.", display=display.none)
pdxAhead   = input.bool(false, "Levels AHEAD of entry only", group=grpPX, tooltip="UNTICKED IS THE DEFAULT SINCE v3.9.8 (\"both sides\"), adopted by user call AGAINST the measurement — tick it to get the v3.9.4-v3.9.7 behaviour back. TICKED: only a level the trade is moving TOWARD can trigger the exit (a rejection at the next obstacle). UNTICKED: a level BEHIND the entry counts too, so closing back through a level the trade had already won is also an exit (\"you lost the level\"). Motivation: on 2026-08-04 and 2026-08-11 the short triggered about 33 cents below PDC and was immediately reclaimed, and ahead-only cannot see that. It does fire on those days (08-04 exits 09:50 for -1.12 instead of 10:05 for -2.45). COST, measured over 2022-01-03..2026-08-10 per unit, unticked vs ticked: A1 485.6 vs 502.0, B1 558.3 vs 575.9, C1 556.4 vs 573.2, D1 480.3 vs 483.5. B1 by year: 2022 -21.2 / 2023 -5.1 / 2024 -4.8 / 2025 -3.4 / 2026 +17.0 — four of five years worse, win rate 46.2% to 44.2%. Only 2026 improves, and 2026 is also the only year the motivating days came from.", display=display.none)

maxCapSL = maxCapOverride > 0 ? maxCapOverride : (isC1 ? 6.0 : 5.0)

// ==================== PRIOR-DAY VOL + DAILY ATR (no repaint) ====================
f_priorRvol() =>
    r = ta.change(close) / close[1] * 100.0
    s = ta.stdev(r, volLookback, false)
    s[1]
rvol20 = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_priorRvol(), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
f_priorATR() =>
    a = ta.sma(ta.tr(true), atrPeriod)
    a[1]
dailyATR = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_priorATR(), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

// ==================== PRIOR-DAY LEVELS (PDH/PDL/PDC/PDO) — DIAGNOSTIC, NOT TRADED ====================
// Yesterday's completed daily bar, held flat across today. Taking [1] INSIDE the request and pairing
// it with lookahead_on is the standard non-repainting idiom (identical to the rvol/ATR calls above):
// it returns the LAST CLOSED daily bar, so today's still-forming O/H/L/C can never leak in.
f_pdLevels() =>
    [open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1]]
[pdO, pdH, pdL, pdC] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_pdLevels(), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

// ==================== "TRADE TASTIC" ATR TRAIL (D1 runner exit) ====================
// ONE line for BOTH directions, exactly the original script: TS = HHV(high - mult*ATR, hhv);
// it MOVES only on a bar that closes above the HHV AND extends (close > prev close) — else it
// holds. Color = close > TS. LONG runner exits on green->red (close <= TS); SHORT runner exits
// on red->green (close > TS) — after a waterfall the falling HHV drags the accepted level down,
// which is how the line comes back under price to catch the cover flip (2026-07-23: flip 10:35
// where the removed "mirror" line exited 11:55). First 16 bars pin to the close (script warm-up).
ttATR = ta.rma(ta.tr(true), ttAtrPeriod)
ttHHV = ta.highest(high - ttMult * ttATR, ttHhvPeriod)
var float ttTS = na
if bar_index < 16
    ttTS := close
else
    ttTS := close > ttHHV and close > close[1] ? ttHHV : ttTS

// ==================== STATE ====================
var float orHigh = na
var float orLow = na
var float orWidth = na
var bool skipVol = false
var bool skipWide = false
var bool daySkipped = false
var bool firstTaken = false
var bool active = false
var int tdir = 0
var float entry = na
var float stop = na
var float tp = na
var int entryBar = na
var bool inRev = false
var bool suppressPartial = false
var bool beTrig = false
var float beLevel = na
var bool part1 = false
var bool vwapArmed = false
var float qtyTotal = na
var float effQty = na
var float part1Pnl = 0.0
var float runnerPeak = na
var int primDir = 0
var bool primStopped = false
var float dayPnl = 0.0
var bool dayHasTrades = false
var int nTrades = 0
var int nSucc = 0
var int nFail = 0
var float netPnl = 0.0
var float grossP = 0.0
var float grossL = 0.0
var float worstDay = na
var float bestDay = na
var int totalDays = 0
var int tradeDays = 0
var int volSkipDays = 0
var int wideSkipDays = 0
var int cStop = 0
var int cWin = 0
var int cEOD = 0
var int cRev = 0
var int cPDX = 0

aPDX = false
aEntryL = false
aEntryS = false
aRevL = false
aRevS = false
aBEFired = false
aPart = false
aWin = false
aStop = false
aEOD = false

// ==================== NEW DAY / OPENING RANGE ====================
isNewDay = session.isfirstbar_regular
isORbar = orStart == "09:45" ? (hour == 9 and minute == 45) : isNewDay
sessVwap = ta.vwap(hlc3, isNewDay)
isEODbar = (hour * 60 + minute) >= (eodHour * 60 + eodMin)
// v3.9.7 HALF-DAY FLATTEN FIX. `session.islastbar_regular` was supposed to cover the early close, and
// it does not — it never fired on TSLA's 12:55 final bar, so the day-after-Thanksgiving sessions
// emitted no EOD exit at all and the position was orphaned into the next day (proven in the v3.9.6
// STRATEGY exports: 2012-11-23, 2017-11-24 and 2018-11-23 all exited a session late, with the
// "EOD flat" safety-net comment rather than "EOD"). Take the session's real end from the daily bar's
// close time: time_close("D") is 13:00 on an early close and 16:00 otherwise, so this fires on the
// genuine last bar of the session, matching orb_engine.py's `last_ts_by_date`. On a full session it
// lands on 15:55, which isEODbar already covered, so normal days are unchanged.
isSessLastBar = not na(time_close("D")) and time_close >= time_close("D")
isLastBar = session.islastbar_regular or isSessLastBar
isFlattenBar = isEODbar or isLastBar

if isNewDay
    if dayHasTrades
        worstDay := na(worstDay) ? dayPnl : math.min(worstDay, dayPnl)
        bestDay := na(bestDay) ? dayPnl : math.max(bestDay, dayPnl)
        tradeDays += 1
    totalDays += 1
    dayPnl := 0.0
    dayHasTrades := false
    orHigh := na
    orLow := na
    orWidth := na
    daySkipped := false
    firstTaken := false
    active := false
    tdir := 0
    entry := na
    stop := na
    tp := na
    entryBar := na
    inRev := false
    suppressPartial := false
    beTrig := false
    beLevel := na
    part1 := false
    vwapArmed := false
    qtyTotal := na
    effQty := na
    part1Pnl := 0.0
    runnerPeak := na
    primDir := 0
    primStopped := false

if isORbar
    orHigh := high
    orLow := low
    orWidth := high - low
    skipVol := not na(rvol20) and rvol20 > maxRvolPct
    skipWide := orWidth > maxORWidth
    daySkipped := skipVol or skipWide
    if skipVol
        volSkipDays += 1
    else if skipWide
        wideSkipDays += 1

longBrk = not na(orHigh) ? orHigh + orWidth * bufferPctOR / 100.0 : na
shortBrk = not na(orLow) ? orLow - orWidth * bufferPctOR / 100.0 : na
tpDist = tpModeSel == "Fixed" ? fixedTP : tpModeSel == "ORw" ? orWidth : tpModeSel == "ATR" ? (not na(dailyATR) ? math.max(atrTPMin, atrTPMult * dailyATR) : fixedTP) : (not na(orWidth) ? math.max(adaptiveTPMin, orWidth * adaptiveTPScale) : na)
canTrade = session.ismarket and not isORbar and not daySkipped and not na(orHigh) and not isFlattenBar and (not entryCutOn or hour * 60 + minute <= entryCutH * 60 + entryCutM)

longConfirm  = not confirmBreakout or (close[1] > longBrk and (close >= open or not requireTrendCandle))
shortConfirm = not confirmBreakout or (close[1] < shortBrk and (close <= open or not requireTrendCandle))

// ==================== PRIMARY ENTRY ====================
if canTrade and not active and not firstTaken
    if close > longBrk and longConfirm
        active := true
        tdir := 1
        inRev := false
        suppressPartial := false
        entry := close
        stop := maxCapSL > 0 ? math.max(orLow, close - maxCapSL) : orLow
        tp := close + tpDist
        beLevel := orHigh - beTrigger * orWidth
        entryBar := bar_index
        qtyTotal := tradeQty
        effQty := tradeQty
        part1 := false
        part1Pnl := 0.0
        beTrig := false
        runnerPeak := na
        vwapArmed := false
        primDir := 1
        firstTaken := true
        aEntryL := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, low, "LONG " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_up, color=color.rgb(7,170,75), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    else if close < shortBrk and shortConfirm
        active := true
        tdir := -1
        inRev := false
        suppressPartial := false
        entry := close
        stop := maxCapSL > 0 ? math.min(orHigh, close + maxCapSL) : orHigh
        tp := close - tpDist
        beLevel := orLow + beTrigger * orWidth
        entryBar := bar_index
        qtyTotal := tradeQty
        effQty := tradeQty
        part1 := false
        part1Pnl := 0.0
        beTrig := false
        runnerPeak := na
        vwapArmed := false
        primDir := -1
        firstTaken := true
        aEntryS := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, high, "SHORT " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_down, color=color.rgb(243,76,76), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)

// ==================== REVERSAL ENTRY ====================
if canTrade and primStopped and not active
    if primDir == 1 and close < orLow
        rpu = math.abs(close - orHigh)
        rq = revRiskCap > 0 and rpu > 0 ? math.min(tradeQty * revQtyMult, revRiskCap / rpu) : tradeQty * revQtyMult
        active := true
        tdir := -1
        inRev := true
        suppressPartial := true
        entry := close
        stop := orHigh
        tp := na
        beLevel := orLow + beTrigger * orWidth
        entryBar := bar_index
        qtyTotal := rq
        effQty := rq
        part1 := false
        part1Pnl := 0.0
        beTrig := false
        runnerPeak := na
        primStopped := false
        cRev += 1
        aRevS := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, high, "REV SHORT " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick) + "\nqty " + str.tostring(rq, "#.##"), style=label.style_label_down, color=color.purple, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    else if primDir == -1 and close > orHigh
        rpu = math.abs(close - orLow)
        rq = revRiskCap > 0 and rpu > 0 ? math.min(tradeQty * revQtyMult, revRiskCap / rpu) : tradeQty * revQtyMult
        active := true
        tdir := 1
        inRev := true
        suppressPartial := true
        entry := close
        stop := orLow
        tp := na
        beLevel := orHigh - beTrigger * orWidth
        entryBar := bar_index
        qtyTotal := rq
        effQty := rq
        part1 := false
        part1Pnl := 0.0
        beTrig := false
        runnerPeak := na
        primStopped := false
        cRev += 1
        aRevL := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, low, "REV LONG " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick) + "\nqty " + str.tostring(rq, "#.##"), style=label.style_label_up, color=color.purple, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)

// ==================== EXIT ENGINE (simulated; stop-first; never on the entry bar) ====================
if active and not na(stop) and bar_index > entryBar
    stopBarStart = stop        // the stop that was actually RESTING coming into this bar
    beFiredNow = false
    // Step 1: BE Retrace
    if not beTrig and not na(beLevel)
        if (tdir == 1 ? low <= beLevel : high >= beLevel)
            stop := tdir == 1 ? math.max(stop, entry) : math.min(stop, entry)
            beTrig := true
            aBEFired := true
            beFiredNow := true
    // Step 2: BE Trail
    if beTrig and beTrailAmt > 0
        stop := tdir == 1 ? math.max(stop, high - beTrailAmt) : math.min(stop, low + beTrailAmt)
    // Step 3: runner level (only after the partial, only for A1/B1/C1)
    runnerHit = false
    float runnerPx = na
    string runnerReason = "Trail"
    if usePartial and part1 and not suppressPartial and isD1
        // D1: TRADE TASTIC color flip — long exits close <= TS (green->red), short close > TS (red->green)
        if tdir == 1 ? close <= ttTS : close > ttTS
            runnerHit := true
            runnerPx := close
            runnerReason := "ATR Trail"
    else if usePartial and part1 and not suppressPartial and runnerVWAP
        if not vwapArmed and (tdir == 1 ? close - entry : entry - close) >= vwapArmProfit
            vwapArmed := true
        if vwapArmed and not na(sessVwap) and (tdir == 1 ? close <= sessVwap : close >= sessVwap)
            runnerHit := true
            runnerPx := close
            runnerReason := "VWAP Cross"
    else if usePartial and part1 and not suppressPartial and not runnerVWAP and runnerMult > 0
        if tdir == 1
            runnerPeak := na(runnerPeak) ? high : math.max(runnerPeak, high)
            lvl = runnerPeak - runnerMult * orWidth
            if exitOnClose ? close <= lvl : low <= lvl
                runnerHit := true
                runnerPx := exitOnClose ? close : lvl
        else
            runnerPeak := na(runnerPeak) ? low : math.min(runnerPeak, low)
            lvl = runnerPeak + runnerMult * orWidth
            if exitOnClose ? close >= lvl : high >= lvl
                runnerHit := true
                runnerPx := exitOnClose ? close : lvl
    // Step 3b: PD-LEVEL TAG-AND-REJECT (v3.9.4; default ON since v3.9.6, both-sides since v3.9.8)
    // — mirrors orb_engine.py `_pd_tag_reject`.
    // Evaluated here but ranked LAST in the elif chain below, so the stop, the target, the partial and
    // the runner all keep precedence and this can only claim a bar none of them wanted.
    bool pdxHit = false
    if pdxOn and not na(entry) and not na(tpDist)
        rngBar = math.max(high - low, syminfo.mintick)
        // small body AND closing against the trade = a doji/pin rejecting the level, not a trend bar
        if (math.abs(close - open) / rngBar) < pdxMaxBody and (tdir == 1 ? close < open : close > open)
            tolPD = pdxZone * tpDist
            usePDO = pdxLevels == "All four (PDO/PDH/PDL/PDC)"
            usePDC = pdxLevels != "PDH + PDL only"
            usePDHL = pdxLevels != "PDC only"
            // v3.9.8: `pdxAhead` off (the new default) drops the "level must lie ahead" guard, so a
            // level BEHIND the entry — one the trade had already won — also triggers on a reclaim.
            if usePDO and not na(pdO) and (not pdxAhead or (pdO - entry) * tdir > 0)
                pdxHit := pdxHit or (tdir == 1 ? (high >= pdO - tolPD and close < pdO) : (low <= pdO + tolPD and close > pdO))
            if usePDHL and not na(pdH) and (not pdxAhead or (pdH - entry) * tdir > 0)
                pdxHit := pdxHit or (tdir == 1 ? (high >= pdH - tolPD and close < pdH) : (low <= pdH + tolPD and close > pdH))
            if usePDHL and not na(pdL) and (not pdxAhead or (pdL - entry) * tdir > 0)
                pdxHit := pdxHit or (tdir == 1 ? (high >= pdL - tolPD and close < pdL) : (low <= pdL + tolPD and close > pdL))
            if usePDC and not na(pdC) and (not pdxAhead or (pdC - entry) * tdir > 0)
                pdxHit := pdxHit or (tdir == 1 ? (high >= pdC - tolPD and close < pdC) : (low <= pdC + tolPD and close > pdC))
    // Step 4: hit checks — STOP FIRST (matches the engine), then target, then partial, then runner
    // resting-stop realism: a BE-retrace that fired THIS bar cannot protect it — fill against the
    // pre-retrace stop (the level actually resting coming into the bar).
    restStop = (beRealistic and beFiredNow) ? stopBarStart : stop
    // Close mode: trigger on the CLOSE beyond the CURRENT stop (be_lag is a wick-only concern), fill at close.
    // Wick mode: trigger on any touch of the be_lag resting stop, fill at the level (gap-aware).
    slHit = exitOnClose ? (tdir == 1 ? close <= stop : close >= stop) : (tdir == 1 ? low <= restStop : high >= restStop)
    slFill = exitOnClose ? close : (tdir == 1 ? math.min(restStop, open) : math.max(restStop, open))
    tpHit = not na(tp) and (tdir == 1 ? high >= tp : low <= tp)

    if slHit
        exitPx = slFill
        perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
        pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty + part1Pnl
        isBETrail = beTrig and (tdir == 1 ? exitPx > entry : exitPx < entry)
        reason = beTrig ? (isBETrail ? "BE Trail" : "BE Stop") : "Base SL"
        cStop += 1
        aStop := true
        nTrades += 1
        if pnlTotal > 0
            nSucc += 1
            grossP += pnlTotal
        else
            nFail += 1
            grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
        netPnl += pnlTotal
        dayPnl += pnlTotal
        dayHasTrades := true
        if not inRev
            // Arms on the STOP-HIT bar (immediate), so the reversal fires on the NEXT bar (N+1) - matches
            // orb_engine.py L933 and the v3 STRATEGY (whose de-sync/arming was reordered 2026-07-13 to also
            // arm on N+1). Base SL / BE Stop / BE Trail arm; peak-trail ("Trail") / VWAP / TP / EOD do not.
            primStopped := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? low : high, (inRev ? "REV " : "") + reason + " " + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n" + (pnlTotal >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=isBETrail ? color.rgb(7,170,75) : color.orange, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        active := false
        tdir := 0
        inRev := false
        tp := na
        stop := na
    else if usePartial and tpHit and not part1
        // D1 full-trail mode: the target touch only ARMS the trail — nothing is closed here
        p1qty = d1FullTrail ? 0.0 : qtyTotal * partialPct / 100.0
        pu = tdir == 1 ? (tp - entry - slippage) : (entry - tp - slippage)
        part1Pnl := pu * p1qty
        effQty := qtyTotal - p1qty
        part1 := true
        if not d1FullTrail
            aPart := true
            if showLabels
                label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, "PARTIAL " + str.tostring(partialPct, "#") + "% @ " + str.tostring(tp, format.mintick) + "\n+" + str.tostring(part1Pnl, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.rgb(7,170,75), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
        else if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, "TRAIL ARMED @ " + str.tostring(tp, format.mintick), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.yellow, 30), textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny)
        tp := na
    else if (not usePartial) and tpHit
        // C2 full exit at the target
        exitPx = tp
        perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
        pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty
        cWin += 1
        aWin := true
        nTrades += 1
        if pnlTotal > 0
            nSucc += 1
            grossP += pnlTotal
        else
            nFail += 1
            grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
        netPnl += pnlTotal
        dayPnl += pnlTotal
        dayHasTrades := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, (inRev ? "REV " : "") + "TP " + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n+" + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.lime, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        active := false
        tdir := 0
        inRev := false
        tp := na
        stop := na
    else if runnerHit
        exitPx = runnerPx
        perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
        pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty + part1Pnl
        cWin += 1
        aWin := true
        nTrades += 1
        if pnlTotal > 0
            nSucc += 1
            grossP += pnlTotal
        else
            nFail += 1
            grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
        netPnl += pnlTotal
        dayPnl += pnlTotal
        dayHasTrades := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, (inRev ? "REV " : "") + runnerReason + " " + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n" + (pnlTotal >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.aqua, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        active := false
        tdir := 0
        inRev := false
        tp := na
        stop := na
    else if pdxHit
        // v3.9.4 PD-level tag-and-reject. Deliberately does NOT set primStopped: only Base SL / BE Stop /
        // BE Trail arm the reversal in orb_engine.py, and this is not a stop-type exit.
        exitPx = close
        perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
        pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty + part1Pnl
        cPDX += 1
        aPDX := true
        nTrades += 1
        if pnlTotal > 0
            nSucc += 1
            grossP += pnlTotal
        else
            nFail += 1
            grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
        netPnl += pnlTotal
        dayPnl += pnlTotal
        dayHasTrades := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, (inRev ? "REV " : "") + "PD Level " + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n" + (pnlTotal >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.purple, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        active := false
        tdir := 0
        inRev := false
        tp := na
        stop := na

// ==================== EOD FORCED CLOSE (all profiles; half-day = session last bar) ====================
if active and isFlattenBar and tdir != 0
    exitPx = close
    perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
    pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty + part1Pnl
    cEOD += 1
    aEOD := true
    nTrades += 1
    if pnlTotal > 0
        nSucc += 1
        grossP += pnlTotal
    else
        nFail += 1
        grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
    netPnl += pnlTotal
    dayPnl += pnlTotal
    dayHasTrades := true
    if showLabels
        label.new(bar_index, close, (inRev ? "REV EOD " : "EOD ") + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n" + (pnlTotal >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.rgb(255,140,0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    active := false
    tdir := 0
    inRev := false
    tp := na
    stop := na

// ==================== VISUALS ====================
// ---- OR / TRIGGER LEVELS (v3.9.5) — one segment per day + a right-end tag, same pattern as the PD lines ----
// v3.9.4 drew these with plot(style_linebr). Even though orHigh/orLow reset to na overnight, a plot is one
// continuous series: TradingView joins the last bar of one session to the first bar of the next, so on a
// multi-day chart the aqua/lime/red levels visibly ran on into the following day. They are now four line
// objects per session, opened on that session's OR bar, extended only to its own bars, and never touched
// again. A small tag ("OR H 331.20", "LONG > 331.55") rides the right end so each line names itself.
cORH = color.new(color.aqua, 0)
cLBK = color.new(color.lime, 0)
cSBK = color.new(color.red, 0)
var line  lnORH = na
var line  lnORL = na
var line  lnLBK = na
var line  lnSBK = na
var label tgORH = na
var label tgORL = na
var label tgLBK = na
var label tgSBK = na
var line[]  orLineHist = array.new_line()
var label[] orTagHist  = array.new_label()

// retire yesterday's four segments on the FIRST bar of the new session, so nothing extends across the gap
// (this must happen at isNewDay, not at the OR bar — with orStart 09:45 the OR bar is three bars late)
if showLevels and isNewDay
    if not na(lnORH)
        array.push(orLineHist, lnORH)
    if not na(lnORL)
        array.push(orLineHist, lnORL)
    if not na(lnLBK)
        array.push(orLineHist, lnLBK)
    if not na(lnSBK)
        array.push(orLineHist, lnSBK)
    if not na(tgORH)
        array.push(orTagHist, tgORH)
    if not na(tgORL)
        array.push(orTagHist, tgORL)
    if not na(tgLBK)
        array.push(orTagHist, tgLBK)
    if not na(tgSBK)
        array.push(orTagHist, tgSBK)
    while array.size(orLineHist) > orKeep * 4
        line.delete(array.shift(orLineHist))
    while array.size(orTagHist) > orKeep * 4
        label.delete(array.shift(orTagHist))
    lnORH := na
    lnORL := na
    lnLBK := na
    lnSBK := na
    tgORH := na
    tgORL := na
    tgLBK := na
    tgSBK := na

// open today's four segments on the OR bar, once the range and the skip decision are both known
if showLevels and isORbar and not daySkipped and not na(orHigh)
    lnORH := line.new(bar_index, orHigh,   bar_index, orHigh,   color=cORH, width=2, style=line.style_solid)
    lnORL := line.new(bar_index, orLow,    bar_index, orLow,    color=cORH, width=2, style=line.style_solid)
    lnLBK := line.new(bar_index, longBrk,  bar_index, longBrk,  color=cLBK, width=1, style=line.style_dashed)
    lnSBK := line.new(bar_index, shortBrk, bar_index, shortBrk, color=cSBK, width=1, style=line.style_dashed)
    if showLvlLbl
        // the two trigger tags sit OUTSIDE the range and the two OR tags INSIDE it, so the pairs never collide
        tgORH := label.new(bar_index, orHigh,   "OR H " + str.tostring(orHigh, format.mintick),   style=label.style_label_up,   color=cORH, textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny)
        tgORL := label.new(bar_index, orLow,    "OR L " + str.tostring(orLow, format.mintick),    style=label.style_label_down, color=cORH, textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny)
        tgLBK := label.new(bar_index, longBrk,  "LONG > " + str.tostring(longBrk, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_down, color=cLBK, textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny)
        tgSBK := label.new(bar_index, shortBrk, "SHORT < " + str.tostring(shortBrk, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_up, color=cSBK, textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)

// extend today's segments (and drag their tags) to the newest bar of THIS session only
if showLevels and session.ismarket
    if not na(lnORH)
        line.set_x2(lnORH, bar_index)
    if not na(lnORL)
        line.set_x2(lnORL, bar_index)
    if not na(lnLBK)
        line.set_x2(lnLBK, bar_index)
    if not na(lnSBK)
        line.set_x2(lnSBK, bar_index)
    if not na(tgORH)
        label.set_x(tgORH, bar_index)
    if not na(tgORL)
        label.set_x(tgORL, bar_index)
    if not na(tgLBK)
        label.set_x(tgLBK, bar_index)
    if not na(tgSBK)
        label.set_x(tgSBK, bar_index)
plot(active ? stop : na, "Active Stop", color=color.red, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(active and not na(tp) ? tp : na, "Active TP", color=color.lime, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(active and not beTrig and not na(beLevel) ? beLevel : na, "BE Trigger", color=color.new(color.yellow, 0), style=plot.style_circles)
plot(primStopped and not active ? (primDir == 1 ? orLow : orHigh) : na, "Reversal Trigger", color=color.new(color.purple, 0), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_circles)
plot(isD1 and active and part1 ? ttTS : na, "ATR Trail (D1 runner)", color=color.new(color.yellow, 0), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr)
bgcolor(daySkipped ? color.new(color.gray, 90) : na, title="Day skipped")

// ---- PRIOR-DAY LEVELS (v3.9.4) — four distinct COLOURS *and* four distinct PATTERNS, per-day segments ----
//   PDH magenta thick solid | PDL blue thick solid | PDC white dotted | PDO orange dashed
cPDH = color.new(color.fuchsia, 0)
cPDL = color.new(color.rgb(41, 98, 255), 0)
cPDC = color.new(color.white, 0)
cPDO = color.new(color.orange, 0)
// v3.9.4: ONE SEGMENT PER DAY. The old plot(style_stepline) ran the whole chart width and drew a
// vertical riser at every session boundary, so yesterday's level bled into today. Now each session opens
// its own four lines on its first RTH bar, extends them only to its own last bar, and never touches the
// next day. Older sessions are deleted once `pdKeep` days are on screen so the 500-object caps are safe.
var line  lnPDH = na
var line  lnPDL = na
var line  lnPDC = na
var line  lnPDO = na
var label tgPDH = na
var label tgPDL = na
var label tgPDC = na
var label tgPDO = na
var line[]  pdLineHist = array.new_line()
var label[] pdTagHist  = array.new_label()

if showPD and isNewDay
    // retire yesterday's four segments (and their tags) into the bounded history ring
    if not na(lnPDH)
        array.push(pdLineHist, lnPDH)
    if not na(lnPDL)
        array.push(pdLineHist, lnPDL)
    if not na(lnPDC)
        array.push(pdLineHist, lnPDC)
    if not na(lnPDO)
        array.push(pdLineHist, lnPDO)
    if not na(tgPDH)
        array.push(pdTagHist, tgPDH)
    if not na(tgPDL)
        array.push(pdTagHist, tgPDL)
    if not na(tgPDC)
        array.push(pdTagHist, tgPDC)
    if not na(tgPDO)
        array.push(pdTagHist, tgPDO)
    while array.size(pdLineHist) > pdKeep * 4
        line.delete(array.shift(pdLineHist))
    while array.size(pdTagHist) > pdKeep * 4
        label.delete(array.shift(pdTagHist))
    // open today's four segments (zero length for now; extended bar by bar below)
    lnPDH := showPDH and not na(pdH) ? line.new(bar_index, pdH, bar_index, pdH, color=cPDH, width=2, style=line.style_solid) : na
    lnPDL := showPDL and not na(pdL) ? line.new(bar_index, pdL, bar_index, pdL, color=cPDL, width=2, style=line.style_solid) : na
    lnPDC := showPDC and not na(pdC) ? line.new(bar_index, pdC, bar_index, pdC, color=cPDC, width=1, style=line.style_dotted) : na
    lnPDO := showPDO and not na(pdO) ? line.new(bar_index, pdO, bar_index, pdO, color=cPDO, width=1, style=line.style_dashed) : na
    // small self-identifying tag, drawn ABOVE the line and carried along to its right end
    tgOn = showPDLbl
    tgPDH := tgOn and showPDH and not na(pdH) ? label.new(bar_index, pdH, "PDH " + str.tostring(pdH, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_down, color=cPDH, textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny) : na
    tgPDL := tgOn and showPDL and not na(pdL) ? label.new(bar_index, pdL, "PDL " + str.tostring(pdL, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_down, color=cPDL, textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny) : na
    tgPDC := tgOn and showPDC and not na(pdC) ? label.new(bar_index, pdC, "PDC " + str.tostring(pdC, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_down, color=cPDC, textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny) : na
    tgPDO := tgOn and showPDO and not na(pdO) ? label.new(bar_index, pdO, "PDO " + str.tostring(pdO, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_down, color=cPDO, textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny) : na

// extend today's segments (and drag their tags) to the newest bar of THIS session only
if showPD
    if not na(lnPDH)
        line.set_x2(lnPDH, bar_index)
    if not na(lnPDL)
        line.set_x2(lnPDL, bar_index)
    if not na(lnPDC)
        line.set_x2(lnPDC, bar_index)
    if not na(lnPDO)
        line.set_x2(lnPDO, bar_index)
    if not na(tgPDH)
        label.set_x(tgPDH, bar_index)
    if not na(tgPDL)
        label.set_x(tgPDL, bar_index)
    if not na(tgPDC)
        label.set_x(tgPDC, bar_index)
    if not na(tgPDO)
        label.set_x(tgPDO, bar_index)

// ==================== ALERTS ====================
if barstate.isconfirmed
    base = " | " + str.substring(profile, 0, 2) + " | " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period + "m | Px $" + str.tostring(close, "#.##") + " | " + str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "America/New_York") + " ET"
    entryShares = math.round(tradeQty * shareQty)
    revShares   = math.round(nz(qtyTotal, tradeQty) * shareQty)        // qtyTotal = risk-parity size on reversal bars
    partShares  = math.round(nz(qtyTotal, tradeQty) * shareQty * partialPct / 100)
    if aEntryL
        alert("[ENTRY] LONG breakout — BUY " + str.tostring(entryShares) + " sh at market" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aEntryS
        alert("[ENTRY] SHORT breakout — SELL SHORT " + str.tostring(entryShares) + " sh at market" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aRevL
        alert("[ENTRY-REV] REVERSAL LONG (risk-parity size) — BUY " + str.tostring(revShares) + " sh at market" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aRevS
        alert("[ENTRY-REV] REVERSAL SHORT (risk-parity size) — SELL SHORT " + str.tostring(revShares) + " sh at market" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aBEFired
        alert("[STATE] BE RETRACE FIRED — move stop to ENTRY" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aPart
        alert("[EXIT-PARTIAL] " + str.tostring(partialPct, "#") + "% closed at target (" + str.tostring(partShares) + " sh); runner now governs" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aWin
        alert("[EXIT-WIN] target / runner exit — close remaining position" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aStop
        alert("[EXIT-STOP] stop hit — close position (Base SL / BE Stop / BE Trail)" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aEOD
        alert("[EXIT-EOD] End-of-day forced close" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aPDX
        alert("[EXIT-PDLEVEL] prior-day level rejected (small-body tag) — close position" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ==================== NAMED ALERTS — per Profile x Status (pick in TradingView's "Add alert" dialog) ==========
// The alert() calls above fire the single generic "Any alert() function call". The alertcondition() calls
// below add NAMED, individually-selectable alerts. Each is gated by the SELECTED profile, so only your active
// profile's alerts can ever fire (on a B1 chart the A1/C1/C2 rows stay silent). Set frequency "Once Per Bar Close".
// --- A1 · Adaptive + Peak-Trail ---
alertcondition(isA1 and aEntryL,  title="A1 Buy",      message="A1 BUY - long breakout, buy at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
